  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191535/rss" title="videojs.org" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;"&gt;What the iPhone Duo Means for Web Development&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The &lt;em&gt;Duo&lt;/em&gt; is out next week, so Darius fired up the simulator to try the Device Posture and Viewport Segments APIs (both available behind a flag). Using Video.js components and CSS, he tried to recreate Netflix's folded-player UI, but Apple's fullscreen restrictions made things a tad interesting.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Darius Cepulis (Video.js) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191536/rss" title="lea.verou.me" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Best Way to Use Icons in Web UIs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Lea shows how to insert and tweak icons without touching &lt;em&gt;any&lt;/em&gt; HTML, using &lt;code&gt;--icon&lt;/code&gt; custom properties, &lt;code&gt;@property&lt;/code&gt;, style queries, and &lt;code&gt;mask&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191573/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The result?&lt;/a&gt; A pure CSS icon system that’s “&lt;em&gt;more flexible and maintainable than what you've been using&lt;/em&gt;”.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Lea Verou &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191534/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/dd0bc385.png" width="135" height="135" style="padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px;     line-height: 100%; "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191534/rss" title="master.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Become the TypeScript Expert on Your Team&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Be the person your team trusts to review AI-generated TypeScript. Learn generics, conditional types, and discriminated unions in depth, then use that knowledge to catch subtle errors and steer AI toward cleaner types.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Master.dev &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

