  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191545/rss" title="calibreapp.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Lazy Loading Images and Media: How Far Ahead Browsers Fetch&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Ben measures how far ahead Chrome, Firefox and Safari fetch lazy-loaded media. He also shares &lt;em&gt;what&lt;/em&gt; we can lazy load (including video and audio in Chromium browsers), and covers where &lt;code&gt;lazy&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;eager&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;fetchpriority&lt;/code&gt; fit.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Ben Schwarz (Calibre) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

